WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.759 --> 00:00:17.460
you show us Morb's contraption?"

2
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:18.721
Venna asked the queen.

3
00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:22.603
"I'm not sure exactly where it is," the queen replied.

4
00:00:22.623 --> 00:00:28.666
"But now I understand why Morb forced me to tell him where he could find the Magica wormholes.

5
00:00:29.286 --> 00:00:31.948
We'll probably find the contraption near one of them."

6
00:00:32.808 --> 00:00:35.829
"You know how to find the wormholes leading to Magica?"

7
00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:36.650
Perda asked.

8
00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:43.073
"As the ruler of this world, I'm the only one who knows the location of every wormhole."

9
00:00:43.693 --> 00:00:46.714
The tiny queen stretched proudly to her full height.

10
00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:53.237
"I'm also the only one with the power to instantly summon every wormhole in Rood to me."

11
00:00:53.257 --> 00:00:55.538
"Really?" Gliss exclaimed.

12
00:00:55.558 --> 00:00:56.979
"Can you do that now?

13
00:00:57.439 --> 00:00:59.360
Summon all the Magica wormholes?

14
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:03.401
Then Morb can't do whatever horrible thing he's planning to do!"

15
00:01:04.602 --> 00:01:06.103
The queen smiled faintly.

16
00:01:06.123 --> 00:01:08.384
"I'm afraid it doesn't work that way.

17
00:01:08.404 --> 00:01:11.645
I can't summon individual wormholes.

18
00:01:12.365 --> 00:01:13.586
Only all of them at once.

19
00:01:14.366 --> 00:01:17.948
We would be overwhelmed by every wormhole to every world there is."

20
00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.929
"Oh." Perda sounded disappointed.

21
00:01:20.949 --> 00:01:22.009
"Too bad."

22
00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:23.870
Zann felt impatient.

23
00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.692
"Then how are we going to get to wherever Morb's new contraption is?"

24
00:01:28.908 --> 00:01:30.369
"Follow me," said the queen.

25
00:01:31.931 --> 00:01:33.192
She started down the hallway.

26
00:01:33.592 --> 00:01:34.813
Zann and the others followed.

27
00:01:35.553 --> 00:01:38.596
"There are multiple wormholes to Magica," Zann said.

28
00:01:38.616 --> 00:01:41.458
"How do you know which one Morb will be near?"

29
00:01:42.139 --> 00:01:46.542
"There's only one Magica wormhole within the walls of this fortress," the queen replied.

30
00:01:46.562 --> 00:01:50.025
"I expect that's the one Morb is planning to use."

31
00:01:51.326 --> 00:01:53.988
As he ran, Zann felt something burning him.

32
00:01:54.769 --> 00:01:57.231
At first he thought it was Zing flying too close.

33
00:01:58.012 --> 00:02:01.177
Then he realized it was the message stone in his pocket.

34
00:02:01.497 --> 00:02:02.618
It was fiery hot.

35
00:02:02.638 --> 00:02:04.379
"Hurry," he urged.

36
00:02:04.399 --> 00:02:05.979
"We must be almost there!"

37
00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:07.120
"We are.

38
00:02:07.420 --> 00:02:08.360
It's just ahead."

39
00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:10.401
The queen led the way through an arch.

40
00:02:11.182 --> 00:02:14.003
Zann followed, and then immediately skidded to a stop.

41
00:02:14.623 --> 00:02:18.365
They were in a stone room with an enormous contraption in the middle.

42
00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:25.168
Like Morb's previous machines, this one was hideous and made up of many different parts.

43
00:02:25.984 --> 00:02:31.088
The first thing Zann noticed was two large, glowing horns sticking out of the top.

44
00:02:31.948 --> 00:02:34.190
The second thing he noticed was his parents.

45
00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:40.094
Their arms and legs were shackled together, and Morb was shoving them up against the terrible machine!

46
00:02:40.114 --> 00:02:42.575
"Stop!" Zann shouted.

47
00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:45.217
"Mom, Dad—it's me!"

48
00:02:45.237 --> 00:02:48.139
"Zann!" his mother cried.

49
00:02:48.159 --> 00:02:51.241
"Zann?" Morb echoed with a scowl.

50
00:02:52.042 --> 00:02:55.444
He gestured to several trolls that were hanging around in the corner.

51
00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.761
"Grab them, you fools!"

52
00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:03.302
Zann tried to duck away, but there was nowhere to run.

53
00:03:04.583 --> 00:03:06.243
The trolls grabbed Zann and the others.

54
00:03:13.105 --> 00:03:15.206
kill them," Morb ordered the trolls.

55
00:03:15.226 --> 00:03:18.287
"Not just yet, anyway."

56
00:03:18.987 --> 00:03:20.027
He smirked at Wyssa.

57
00:03:20.047 --> 00:03:22.748
"I didn't expect to see you again."

58
00:03:23.616 --> 00:03:26.017
He widened his gaze to include all of them.

59
00:03:26.037 --> 00:03:28.858
"Or any of you, for that matter.

60
00:03:29.559 --> 00:03:33.881
But now that you're here, I hope you'll stick around and enjoy the show."

61
00:03:34.801 --> 00:03:36.782
Zann heard Wyssa muttering under her breath.

62
00:03:37.602 --> 00:03:38.483
Morb heard it too.

63
00:03:38.503 --> 00:03:42.464
"Let me guess," Morb sneered.

64
00:03:42.484 --> 00:03:48.127
"You're planning to try some powerful, little-known spell you've learned during your travels.

65
00:03:48.907 --> 00:03:50.808
Don't bother—it's too late.

66
00:03:51.656 --> 00:03:54.877
My new pets have already latched onto their victims."

67
00:03:55.997 --> 00:03:57.798
He waved a hand toward the contraption.

68
00:03:58.478 --> 00:04:04.060
Tiny creatures, hundreds of them, were swarming out of a tank in the center of the contraption.

69
00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:08.701
The creatures looked like small, brightly colored cave crawlers.

70
00:04:09.581 --> 00:04:13.842
Zann gasped in horror as the small rodents scampered all over his parents.

71
00:04:14.802 --> 00:04:15.863
"Memory mice!"

72
00:04:16.163 --> 00:04:16.843
Wyssa spat.

73
00:04:16.863 --> 00:04:17.863
"Of course!

74
00:04:18.023 --> 00:04:19.864
I should have guessed you'd use them."

75
00:04:20.488 --> 00:04:21.729
"What are memory mice?"

76
00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:22.610
Darb asked.

77
00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:26.253
"They feed on people's memories," Wyssa said.

78
00:04:26.273 --> 00:04:31.738
"Their feeding has the side effect of creating very strong magical energy."

79
00:04:31.758 --> 00:04:34.320
"They eat memories?"

80
00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:35.521
Gliss frowned.

81
00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.023
"How awful!"

82
00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:39.645
"Not necessarily," said Wyssa.

83
00:04:39.665 --> 00:04:43.668
"In their home world, they're a beloved and valuable species.

84
00:04:44.429 --> 00:04:47.472
They help people by deleting painful memories.

85
00:04:48.364 --> 00:04:53.886
They also create much useful energy out of useless or unwanted memories."

86
00:04:54.946 --> 00:04:57.687
Zann struggled to free himself from the troll holding him.

87
00:04:57.707 --> 00:04:59.987
"Mom, Dad!"

88
00:05:00.247 --> 00:05:00.667
he called.

89
00:05:00.688 --> 00:05:05.909
"I'm afraid your parents can't answer you, boy," Morb said.

90
00:05:05.929 --> 00:05:10.890
"They're busy right now—having all their memories devoured."

91
00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:16.332
"Like anything," Wyssa went on, "memory mice can be used for evil."

92
00:05:17.236 --> 00:05:19.118
She shot Morb a disgusted look.

93
00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:25.864
"Normally a person must invite the mice to latch on, and they only feed for a limited amount

94
00:05:25.904 --> 00:05:26.464
of time.

95
00:05:27.545 --> 00:05:31.869
Morb must have overridden that instinct with some kind of spell."

96
00:05:31.889 --> 00:05:34.171
"Clever, isn't it?"

97
00:05:34.551 --> 00:05:35.532
Morb smiled.

98
00:05:35.552 --> 00:05:40.717
"My Memory Machine can use any memories to summon the power it needs.

99
00:05:41.698 --> 00:05:43.960
I could have used my Roodian servants.

100
00:05:44.964 --> 00:05:48.246
Even trolls' feeble brains have enough memories to work."

101
00:05:48.986 --> 00:05:49.487
He chuckled.

102
00:05:50.947 --> 00:05:55.370
"But I liked the irony of using Magica memories to destroy Magica.

103
00:05:56.130 --> 00:05:59.232
Besides, I already had these two as my prisoners.

104
00:05:59.932 --> 00:06:03.414
They were very useful in helping me find my way to Rood."

105
00:06:04.715 --> 00:06:09.038
"Your only true talent is holding a grudge," Wyssa retorted.

106
00:06:09.058 --> 00:06:13.140
"It's not Nax and Asta's fault you were born a Void."

107
00:06:13.916 --> 00:06:14.817
Morb ignored her.

108
00:06:14.837 --> 00:06:16.698
"I'm glad you're here, Zann.

109
00:06:17.418 --> 00:06:19.699
Perhaps you can be useful to me at last.

110
00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:24.682
I've ordered the mice to drain your parents of all memories of Magica.

111
00:06:25.402 --> 00:06:32.326
If that's not enough to fill the machine He touched a large clear tube on one side, which

112
00:06:32.366 --> 00:06:35.808
was rapidly filling with glowing, sparking magic energy.

113
00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:41.091
"Well, then perhaps I'll have to top it off with your memories."

114
00:06:41.111 --> 00:06:43.432
"No!" Zann blurted out.

115
00:06:44.404 --> 00:06:45.585
"Wait," Perda said.

116
00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:47.727
"What happens when the tube is full?"

117
00:06:47.747 --> 00:06:53.671
"Why, then all I have to do is open this hatch," said Morb, smiling wickedly.

118
00:06:53.691 --> 00:06:58.174
"The energy will get sucked through any wormhole within range.

119
00:06:59.095 --> 00:07:05.019
As it happens, the only wormhole in this room leads directly into Wyssa's old home of Wormwood."

120
00:07:05.860 --> 00:07:06.820
Venna looked nervous.

121
00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.321
"And then what happens?"

122
00:07:08.341 --> 00:07:11.784
"Then the energy will explode," Morb said.

123
00:07:12.332 --> 00:07:15.920
"Blowing all of Magica to smithereens!"
